On Thu, Apr 2, 2015 at 12:28 AM, guskant <gusni.kantu@gmail.com> wrote:

>
> However, in considering the definitions of cmavo using {ze'ei}, I am
> inclined to make it of selma'o {GOI} rather than {MAI}.
> It is because definitions like {iu bu ze'ei ku} are not grammatical. There
> are many cmavo that cannot stand alone. Those cmavo should be defined with
> a statement, not with an expanded form of the defined cmavo.
>
> Using {ze'ei} of GOI, the definition of {xo'e} will be:
>
> zo pa ze'ei zo zo'e
>

I thought the point of "ze'ei" was to create members of any selma'o, like
BU does for selma'o BY and ZEI for BRIVLA, not to define new words. I'm not
sure I see the point of having a cmavo dedicated to one-word definitions.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

